{"parentUuid":"5a86baab-b13f-4de4-9ab4-da9a9bfff923","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01BKy3or1wgQT4AqFwvTUQst","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Claude Code in VSCode and the Claude CLI are **separate processes with isolated session contexts** — they don't share conversation history by design.\n\nKey reasons:\n\n1. **No shared session store** — conversation history lives in-memory per process. There's no persistent shared file the extension can read from.\n\n2. **Different entry points** — the VSCode extension spawns its own Claude Code process; the terminal CLI is a different process entirely. Neither knows about the other's sessions.\n\n3. **No cross-instance sync** — Anthropic hasn't built a mechanism to sync session history across instances (CLI, VS Code, JetBrains, web).\n\n**What you can do to bridge sessions:**\n\n- Use `memory-keeper` or `mcp-project-context` (you have both configured) to persist context that can be rehydrated in any session.\n- Use `/compact` or save explicit handoff notes so you can paste context into a new session.\n- CLAUDE.md (your global config) is loaded in all sessions, so durable preferences/policies survive across instances automatically.\n\nThe short answer: session history is ephemeral and per-process — the extension and CLI simply don't share a history backend."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11600,"cache_read_input_tokens":11296,"output_tokens":402,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11600,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CZY8Av5bL3HdyB4PGHmsP","type":"assistant","uuid":"6d4ed7fc-90c0-4ce8-89ad-016420b437d3","timestamp":"2026-03-29T22:01:17.522Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/testuser",